import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
lines = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 665 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1
lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, "| 666 | 2026-10-26 | **Playing Scales, chapter 18 (Build AB; the syllabus check's build order, item 2).** Built on row 665. A technique room after Scales on the Prelim - Grade 1 floor: the Scales room says which fingers, this one plays them. Five steps, each with its pad: (1) Smooth turns: the hand as five finger circles that glide when the thumb passes under or 3 crosses over; a smooth scale and a bumpy one (the note after the turn late and loud) to hear and tell apart. (2) On the beat: C and G major, each hand, four clicks then one note a click up and back, the last note two beats; play along on the screen's keys, scored; 60 then 76. (3) A and E minor, natural then harmonic (the 7th up a half step), C major's fingers; natural or harmonic by ear. (4) Mirror twins: contrary motion, both thumbs on middle C (C major) or the A below (A harmonic minor), the same finger numbers both ways, 66; tap the left hand's key. (5) Two octaves, hands together (Grade 1: G, F, E minor, D minor): a strip with the right hand's fingers above and the left hand's below, two notes a beat (run-ning), find where both thumbs play together (G: the middle G only; F: C, F, C). Fingerings and speeds checked against the technical work book pages (P.1 to P.8, 1.1 to 1.10). Drill: six levels (which finger, one octave; natural or harmonic; mirror twins; which finger, two octaves; listen: smooth or bumpy; listen: natural or harmonic). Home: the Technique door's 'Playing scales and chords' opens with the five lessons; the fingerings in every key follow. Book: 7 pages (a drawn crotchet in metronome marks). Not yet: Workbook and teacher's copy; broken triads wait for the board's call 13. Files: drills.html, drills.src.html, _workspace/concept-book-kit/sc/patch690.py (+ spx.jsx, sph.jsx). |")
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
